=== SIGNATURE ===
rotate_arrow(arrow, steps, [clockwise], [as_num])

=== COMMENT ===
Rotates an arrow by 45 degrees times steps. arrow may be a standard arrow, its numeric equivalent, or a letter code (U D L R UL UR DL DR). clockwise = 1 (default) rotates clockwise, 0 counter-clockwise. as_num = 0 (default) returns an arrow, 1 returns the numeric equivalent.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(arrow, steps, [clockwise], [as_num], LET(
   arrows, "↑↗→↘↓↙←↖",
   arrow_list, MID(arrows, SEQUENCE(8), 1),
   idx, XMATCH(z_dir_to_arrow(arrow), arrow_list),
   turn, IF(ISOMITTED(clockwise), steps, IF(OR(clockwise = 0, clockwise = "ccw"), -steps, steps)),
   pos, MOD(idx - 1 + turn, 8) + 1,
   out, IFNA(MID(arrows, pos, 1), ""),
   IF(IF(ISOMITTED(as_num), 0, as_num) = 1, z_arrow_to_num(out), out)
))

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Rotates an arrow around the eight compass directions.

Arguments:
  arrow       - the arrow to rotate: a standard arrow (↑↗→↘↓↙←↖), its numeric equivalent (1, -1000000, ...), or a letter code (U D L R UL UR DL DR).
  steps       - number of 45-degree turns.
  [clockwise] - 1 = clockwise (default), 0 = counter-clockwise (the string "ccw" also means counter-clockwise).
  [as_num]    - 0 = return the arrow glyph (default), 1 = return its numeric equivalent.

Returns:
  The rotated arrow (or, with as_num = 1, its numeric equivalent), or "" if arrow is not one of the eight directions.

Example:
  rotate_arrow("→", 1)         ->  "↘"
  rotate_arrow("→", 1, 0)      ->  "↗"
  rotate_arrow("→", 1, 1, 1)   ->  1000001   (the number for ↘)
  rotate_arrow(1, 2)           ->  "↓"       (1 is →, two turns clockwise)
